<!-- ascribe:agents:docs start (generated by `ascribe agents sync`; edit docs/ascribe.toml, not this block) -->
## Ascribe documentation in `docs/`

The Markdown pages under `docs/content/` are Ascribe documentation: pages with YAML frontmatter, `@` directives, and `{key}` phrases, checked against the content model in `docs/ascribe.toml`. This project's rules are in `docs/AGENTS.md`: read them before editing a page there.

Programmatic check: after editing a page, run `ascribe check <file> --format concise` and fix every error. Before you finish, run `ascribe check --config docs`. `ascribe explain <code>` says what a problem means and how to fix it.
<!-- ascribe:agents:docs end -->

