## Ascribe documentation in `handbook/`

The Markdown pages under `handbook/pages/` are Ascribe documentation: pages with YAML frontmatter, `@` directives, and `{key}` phrases, checked against the content model in `handbook/ascribe.toml`. The pages under `handbook/pages/security/` aren't: that folder is another project's, with its own `ascribe.toml` and rules. This project's rules are in `handbook/AGENTS.md`: read them before editing a page there.

Programmatic check: after editing a page, run `ascribe check <file> --format concise` and fix every error. Before you finish, run `ascribe check --config handbook`. `ascribe explain <code>` says what a problem means and how to fix it.
<!-- ascribe:agents:handbook end -->

